      ],
      "source": "https://www.delawarecountyhistory.com/eastlansdowneborough/"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "East Lansdowne takes its name from the neighboring borough of Lansdowne located just to the west.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.delawarecountyhistory.com/eastlansdowneborough/"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Unlike many nearby towns, East Lansdowne was bought as a single family farm specifically for residential development.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
